        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Workers in a coffee plantation take 18 days to pick coffee berries in 20% of the plantation. How many days will they take to complete the picking work for the entire plantation, assuming the rate of work stays the same? Why is this assumption necessary?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.174,
            0.711,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. The badminton coach has planned the training sessions such that the ratio of warm up : play : cool down is 10% : 80% : 10%. If he wants to conduct a training of 90 minutes. How long should each activity be done?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.737,
            0.175,
            0.836,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.737,
                0.175,
                0.836,
                0.274
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.277,
            0.847,
            0.335
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. An estimated 90% of the world’s population lives in the Northern Hemisphere. Find the (approximate) number of people living in the Northern Hemisphere based on this year’s worldwide population."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.343,
            0.847,
            0.399
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. A recipe for the dish, halwa, for 4 people has the following ingredients in the given proportions — Rava: 40%, Sugar: 40%, and Ghee: 20%."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.41,
            0.845,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) If you want to make halwa for 8 people, what is the proportion of each of the above ingredients?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.452,
            0.845,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) If the total weight of the ingredients is 2 kg, how much rava, sugar and ghee are present?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.51,
            0.453,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.3 Using Percentages"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.546,
            0.454,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To Compare Proportions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.57,
            0.847,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Eesha scored 42 marks out of 50 on an English test and 70 marks out of 80 in a Science test. Since she lost only 8 marks in English but 10 marks in Science, she thinks she has done better at English. Reema does not agree! She argues that since Eesha has scored more marks in Science, she has done better at Science. Vishu thinks we cannot compare the scores because the maximum marks are different. Who do you think is correct?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.704,
            0.846,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the maximum marks are the same, the comparison becomes easier, isn’t it? For these kinds of comparisons, we need to convert both values to percentages."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.762,
            0.604,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "English score as a percentage "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{42}{50} \\times 100 = 84\\%"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.792,
            0.624,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Science score as a percentag "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{e}=\\frac{70}{80} \\times 100=87.5\\%."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.819,
            0.846,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Science score (as a percentage) is higher than the English score (as a percentage). So, we can conclude that Eesha has scored better on the Science test."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
